Rasperry device tree was changed USB device tree part from 4.9 -> 4.19 in an incompatible way:
 interrupts = <2 0>, <1 9>; -> interrupts = <1 9>, <2 0>;

This break usb, especially ethernet support denying access to eth0 to verify device-label.
Kernel 4.19 uses interrupt-names, thus it is safe to change the order back to 4.9 way and
adjust names accordingly.

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/bcm270x.dtsi b/arch/arm/boot/dts/bcm270x.dtsi
index 9eb6bec..3b00f2e 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/bcm270x.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/bcm270x.dtsi
@@ -131,10 +131,10 @@
 			compatible = "brcm,bcm2708-usb";
 			reg = <0x7e980000 0x10000>,
 			      <0x7e006000 0x1000>;
-			interrupt-names = "usb",
-					  "soft";
-			interrupts = <1 9>,
-				     <2 0>;
+			interrupt-names = "soft",
+					  "usb";
+			interrupts = <2 0>,
+				     <1 9>;
 		};
 
 		v3d@7ec00000 { /* vd3 */
